{
  "name": "Gerbil Scheme",
  "description": "Gerbil is a high-performance, systems-oriented dialect of Scheme that extends the Gambit runtime with a sophisticated macro and module system. It features a native implementation of syntax-case and a full meta-syntactic tower, enabling advanced metaprogramming while maintaining efficient ahead-of-time compilation via single-instantiation modules. The project provides an extensive standard library supporting actor-oriented distributed programming, database interfacing, and low-level POSIX systems integration.",
